nodes.prompt:
You are building an “Email Drip Campaign System” addendum to an existing Business + Marketing Plan for {business_name} / {brand_name}.

First, lock the operating context:
- Owner: {owner_name}
- Offers: {primary_offers}
- Service area: {service_area}
- Voice: {voice_guidelines}
- Booking link: {booking_link}
- CRM: {crm_name}
- Compliance notes: {compliance_notes}

If {trigger_sources_table} is provided, use it as the source-to-sequence mapping. If it is missing, propose a reasonable mapping based on the offers and channels.

Output:
1) A short “Why this drip exists” paragraph (trust-building touches, not one follow-up)
2) The 6-stage framework labels: welcome, education, social proof, soft ask, urgency nudge, re-engagement
3) The exact 30-day cadence (Day 0, 2, 5, 10, 17, 30) with a one-line goal for each touch

Keep tone plain-English and client-trust focused. No hype.
